## Bids

data bids = bidder,size kW,price,25-year savings,warranty years,complete by,net benefit; Copperfield Solar,1250,2875000,7900000,25,2027-07-31,5025000; SunHarvest,1200,2640000,7400000,25,2027-08-15,4760000; Meridian Renewables,1200,2400000,7150000,15,2027-08-31,4750000; Brightline Energy,1150,2415000,7050000,20,2027-09-30,4635000; Halcyon Power,1100,2640000,6800000,30,2027-10-31,4160000

table bids cols=bidder,size kW,price,25-year savings,warranty years title="Five bids, price and savings in dollars"

## Net benefit

Net 25-year benefit is savings minus price.

chart hbar bids x=bidder y=net benefit unit=$ labels focus="Copperfield Solar" title="Net 25-year benefit"

## Schedule fit

Panels must be generating before the school year starts on 2027-09-01.

table bids cols=bidder,complete by sort=complete by

!! Brightline Energy (2027-09-30) and Halcyon Power (2027-10-31) would finish after the school year starts.

## Recommendation

Choose Copperfield Solar. It has the highest net benefit, 265000 dollars above SunHarvest, and the earliest completion, 2027-07-31.

!! Copperfield also has the highest upfront price, 2875000 dollars, which the district must finance.
